sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as ListsHandler<br/>src/App/App.Host/Api/Cli/Endpoint/ListsHandler.cs
    participant Handler as CompleteItemHandler<br/>src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application/Commands/CompleteItemHandler.cs
    participant Repository as IRepository of Item<br/>src/Infrastructure/Postgres/Postgres/Repositories/PostgresRepository.cs
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Client->>+Handler: CompleteItemCommand(home, 1, version "7") from lists complete --list home --id 1 --version 7
    Handler->>+Repository: FirstOrDefaultAsync(ItemOfListById), untracked
    Repository->>+DB: SELECT id, list_id, title, done, xmin FROM list_items
    DB-->>-Repository: the row, xmin 9: another caller changed it
    Repository-->>-Handler: Item, Version 9
    Note over Handler: item.Complete(), then item.ChangeUnder("7"): the caller's, not 9
    Handler->>+Repository: UpdateAsync(item at version 7)
    Repository->>+DB: UPDATE ... WHERE id = 1 AND xmin = 7 RETURNING xmin
    DB-->>-Repository: no row: DbUpdateConcurrencyException
    Repository-->>-Handler: DbUpdateConcurrencyException
    Note over Handler: the store failures middleware answers it:<br/>ConcurrentChange, "item was changed meanwhile"
    Handler-->>-Client: exit 2, concurrent change: read it again
